      "id": "a1",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:00:12Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "The retries come from `deliver` in the webhook sender. Each failure puts the delivery back at the head of the queue, so one dead endpoint holds every slot."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "reasoning",
      "id": "r1",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:00:18Z",
      "text": "The backoff never grows: a failed webhook waits a flat second and goes again. Doubling it from one second to a minute frees the slots."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "calls",
     "id": "t2",
     "names": [
      "Edit",
      "Bash"
     ],
     "rows": [
      {
       "kind": "tool",
       "id": "t2",
       "at": "2026-11-11T03:00:20Z",
       "text": "Edit crates/fleet/src/deliver.rs"
      },
      {
       "kind": "tool",
       "id": "t2b",
       "at": "2026-11-11T03:00:30Z",
       "text": "Bash armada check test deliver"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f0",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:00:40Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "The delivery loop now reads its next attempt from the backoff, and a failure moves the delivery to the back of the queue rather than the head."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f1",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:01:00Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "you"
      },
      "text": "What happens to deliveries already waiting when Fleet restarts?"
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f2",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:01:20Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "They are read back from the store with the attempt count they had. The first attempt after a restart waits the backoff that count gives, so a restart does not start a burst."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f3",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:01:40Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "you"
      },
      "text": "And a delivery that keeps failing for a day?"
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f4",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:02:00Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "It stops at the minute ceiling and keeps trying once a minute. Nothing is dropped. The Jobs list shows the endpoint as failing after ten attempts in a row."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f5",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:02:20Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "you"
      },
      "text": "Show me the test that holds the ceiling."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f6",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:02:40Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "`deliver::tests::backoff_stops_at_a_minute` runs twenty failures and reads each wait: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 32s, then 60s for the rest."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f7",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:03:00Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "you"
      },
      "text": "Does the order of deliveries to one endpoint still hold?"
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
      "kind": "message",
      "id": "f8",
      "at": "2026-11-11T03:03:20Z",
      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "Yes. Deliveries to one endpoint wait behind the first one that failed, so they arrive in the order they were made. Other endpoints are not held up by it."
     }
    },
    {
     "kind": "row",
     "row": {
